      "description": "Watch DC United vs Toronto FC highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 26, 2026. The atmosphere was electric for this MLS clash on 2026-07-26, as two sides prepared to battle for vital points in the mid-season standings. DC United and Toronto FC squared off in a match that promised high-stakes drama, with both managers looking to exploit tactical gaps from the opening whistle. A Cruel Twist in the First Half The opening period was a cagey affair, defined by midfield duels and disciplined defensive lines. However, the deadlock was broken in the 41st minute through a moment of pure misfortune for the visitors. Kobe Franklin inadvertently directed the ball into his own net, gifting DC United a 1-0 lead. The own goal acted as a catalyst for the game, forcing Toronto FC to abandon their conservative approach as they headed into the halftime break searching for answers. Toronto's Resilience and the Equalizer The second half saw a flurry of substitutions as both teams looked to refresh their lineups. The introduction of Djordje Mihailovic for the visitors added a new dimension to their attack, and their persistence finally paid off in the 76th minute. Theodor Corbeanu found space in the final third and clinicaly finished to level the score at 1-1. The tension escalated quickly following the equalizer, with yellow cards shown to Louis Munteanu and Jonathan Osorio as the physical battle intensified heading into the closing stages. Stoppage Time Drama Just as it seemed the points would be shared, the match delivered a final, breathtaking twist deep into injury time. In the 100th minute, DC United were awarded a penalty, sending the home crowd into a frenzy. Tai Baribo stepped up to the spot under immense pressure and calmly converted, making it 2-1. It was a heart-stopping conclusion to a fixture that remained undecided until the very last kick, leaving the visitors empty-handed despite a spirited comeback."
